  "docTitle": "Live Streaming (Twitch / Live Cricket) - SDE Prep Dojo",
  "description": "Design a live streaming platform like Twitch or live cricket: RTMP/SRT ingest, real-time ABR transcoding, low-latency HLS/DASH through a CDN, how live differs from VOD, match subscriptions with signed expiring playback links, match-start traffic spikes, and a concurrent-viewer counter.",
  "hero": {
    "tag": "header",
    "attrs": {
      "class": "page-hero"
    },
    "html": "\n        <div class=\"hero-meta\">\n          <span class=\"level-badge\" data-level=\"5\">Level 5 - Interview-ready</span>\n          <span class=\"time\">35 min</span>\n          <span class=\"chip company\">Oracle</span><span class=\"chip company\">Zepto</span><span class=\"chip company\">JioHotstar</span>\n          <span class=\"chip kafka\">Kafka</span><span class=\"chip k8s\">Kubernetes</span>\n        </div>\n        <h1>Live Streaming (Twitch / Live Cricket)</h1>\n        <p class=\"lead\">Follow one live video frame from a streamer's camera to 50 million phones a few seconds later: ingest, real-time transcoding, low-latency HLS through a CDN, signed links that expire, surviving the traffic wall when a cricket match starts, and counting who is watching - as asked by Oracle, Zepto and JioHotstar.</p>\n      "
